Subject: [PATCH 1/3] docs: a claim comment is a claim - mirror it as a label,
 both ways

Only collaborators can set labels, so anyone else claims an issue by
commenting `claimed:` (or `/claim`). AGENTS.md now says the comment is
the claim and the label only mirrors it: check comments before claiming,
label an unlabelled comment claim (plus the assignee), and drop the
label when the claim comment is deleted or the claimant says unclaim.
A contributor's claim stands while its comment exists (no 4 h timer;
agent claims keep the 4 h rule). /review-prs step 4 now syncs both ways.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
